.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt RSH 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm rsh
.Nd the RavenBSD shell
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Ar script
.Nm
.Fl c Ar command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the first shell of RavenBSD.
It opens
.Pa tty:console
(it needs the console server,
.Xr consd 8 ) ,
prints the prompt
.Dq Li "raven# "
and evaluates one line at a time.
Commands run against the
.Pa file:
namespace
.Xr vfsd 8
mounts, so
.Pa /
is the read-only initfs and
.Pa /tmp
is the in-memory filesystem of
.Xr ramfsd 8 .
.Pp
The command line supports words with single quotes, double quotes and backslash escapes,
.Ic #
comments, the connectors
.Ic \&;
.Ic &&
and
.Ic ||
and the redirections
.Ic > ,
.Ic >>
and
.Ic <
(redirections are implemented for builtins only).
Variable expansion understands
.Va $NAME ,
.Va ${NAME}
and
.Va $? .
There is no globbing, no history, no completion, no pipes and no job control; a pipe is reported
as
.Dq Li "rsh: pipes are not supported yet" .
.Sh BUILTINS
.Bl -tag -width "export" -compact
.It Ic cd Ar dir
Change the shell's working directory.
.It Ic pwd
Print the working directory.
.It Ic echo Ar words...
Print the words, or write them to the redirection target.
.It Ic exit Op Ar n
Exit the shell with status
.Ar n
(the default is the last status).
.It Ic set
Print every variable as
.Va NAME=value .
.It Ic export Op Ar NAME[=value] ...
Mark variables for children, optionally setting them.
.It Ic unset Ar NAME ...
Remove variables.
.It Ic env
Print the exported variables.
.It Ic help
List the builtins.
.It Ic type Ar name
Explain whether a name is a builtin or where it resolves.
.El
.Sh EXTERNAL COMMANDS
A word without a slash is looked up in
.Pa /bin
and then
.Pa /sbin ;
a word with a slash is used as given.
The program is loaded from the initfs with
.Xr spawn 2 ,
receives the words as arguments and the exported variables plus
.Va PWD
as its environment, and
.Nm
waits for it (see
.Xr proc_wait 2 ) ,
setting
.Va $?
to its exit status.
An unknown command reports
.Dq Li "rsh: name: command not found"
and sets
.Va $?
to 127.
.Pp
At startup
.Nm
prints
.Dq Li "rsh: ready"
and runs
.Pa /etc/rc.local
when that file exists.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/rsh.toml
Service manifest: needs
.Nm consd ,
.Nm vfsd ,
.Nm ramfsd
and
.Nm initfsd ,
grants the initfs, and never restarts.
.It Pa /etc/rc.local
Optional startup script.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits with the status of its last command, or with the argument of
.Ic exit .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr consd 8 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr vfsd 8
